<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shams al-Din Muhammad Kart</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1278</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Shams al-Din Kart</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shams al-Din Muhammad Kart was the first malik of the Kart dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herat">Herat</a>, of a family linked to the Ghurid Sultanate. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> appointed him ruler of Herat around 1245, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongke">Great Khan Möngke</a> confirmed him. He rebuilt the city after its destruction by the Mongols and extended his authority over neighbouring regions, but was poisoned in 1278 on the orders of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhan">Ilkhan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abaqa-khan">Abaqa</a>.</p></div>
